{"name":"Underpass Shrine","hex":"#cc4422","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"underpass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A passage, especially for pedestrians, that crosses underneath a road, railroad or obstacle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/underpass"},{"term":"shrine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A holy or sacred place dedicated to a specific deity, ancestor, hero, martyr, saint, or similar figure of awe and respect, at which said figure is venerated or worshipped.","A case, box, or receptacle, especially one in which are deposited sacred relics, as the bones of a saint."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enshrine; to place reverently, as if in a shrine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Subway (crossing)","blocks":[{"text":"A subway, also known as an underpass, is a grade-separated pedestrian crossing running underneath a road or railway in order to entirely separate pedestrians and cyclists from motor or train traffic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Praha%2C_Fugnerovo_n%C3%A1m%C4%9Bst%C3%AD%2C_podchod_pod_Sokolskou.ogv/330px--Praha%2C_Fugnerovo_n%C3%A1m%C4%9Bst%C3%AD%2C_podchod_pod_Sokolskou.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subway_(crossing)"},{"title":"Shrine","blocks":[{"text":"A shrine is a sacred space dedicated to a specific deity, ancestor, hero, martyr, saint, daemon, or similar figure of respect, wherein they are venerated and/or worshipped. Shrines often contain idols, relics, or other such objects associated with the figure being venerated. A shrine at which votive offerings are made is called an altar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Gorskii_03982u.jpg/330px-Gorskii_03982u.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrine"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w